What the new bytes change
-------------------------
  `diff` of the 6245117d… copy against this one is five hunks. Four are yaml
  comments (the acceptance-count note, "binary_opcodes == 17", the "Binary
  opcodes (17 = …)" header, and the fp_arith comment). The fifth deletes
  the `frem` row: f16/f32/f64/f80 x 15 variants = 60 cq_template_frem_*
  symbols. Nothing else in the grid moves. The opcode grid goes from 2,479
  to 2,419 symbols, and the whole cq_template_* surface from 2,880 to 2,820.

  Every one of the 60 was a LOUD ABORT in libcqops before this re-vendor
  (shim/gen_reasons.py: no soft_frem construction in the pinned Bennett
  snapshot), so no capability is lost.

  The yaml's lines 62-203 moved down by ONE (the acceptance-count note is
  two lines where it was one) and every line from 204 on is where it was.
  Bare line citations into this file in that range now point one line
  early.

Verification of the copy
------------------------
  sha256 of `git show 4266c40d:tools/opcode_table.yaml` and of this copy are
  identical, and equal to `git show 61999c4a:tools/opcode_table.yaml`.

  The sha256 is independently corroborated INSIDE CQ_lang: the generated
  header carries it in its banner —
    runtime/cq_templates.h:1 at 4266c40d (unchanged since 61999c4a)
    /* AUTOGENERATED - do not edit. yaml-sha256: 7307995f...6f8322 */
  so this copy is the exact revision that produced the shipped
  runtime/cq_templates.h, which declares 2,419 cq_template_* symbols. Its
  declarations are the old header's 2,479 minus exactly the 60
  cq_template_frem_*, in the same order. CQ_lang's own generator,
  tools/gen_templates.py at 4266c40d, was copied to a SCRATCH directory with
  its helper abi_codegen.py and run over the three vendored yamls with a
  scratch --output-dir: the cq_templates.h it wrote is byte-identical to
  CQ_lang's committed header, and its cq_link_smoke.c asserts
  `cq_link_smoke_count == 2820UL`. Nothing was run inside CQ_lang.

